  "research_id": "federal-science-operating-system",
  "title": "Federal Science Operating System",
  "question": "How does federal science doctrine move through mission selection, capital, security gates, industrial capability and operation without collapsing strategy into delivery?",
  "bluf": "The doctrine-to-operation map for an AI-native scientific-industrial economy now includes an international endorsement layer. On October 4, the United States and sixteen other countries endorsed the Kyoto Vision's portfolio of long-duration and rapid grants, prizes, new research institutions, government metascience capability, Super Intelligence for closed-loop discovery, access to data/compute/facilities and technical-talent pathways. This confirms international uptake of the July U.S. design doctrine, but the one-page declaration sends implementation back into national systems and creates no common institution, fund, programme, access right, deadline or reporting mechanism. The August NSSTS security membrane and the fusion implementation gates remain separate U.S. layers.",
  "evidence_cutoff": "2026-10-04",
  "evidence_cutoff_note": "The original system map retains its August 17 evidence boundary. September 7 targeted factual-spine additions reconcile the Reactor filings, September 9 adds the bounded Genesis update, and October 4 adds the Kyoto Vision international-endorsement audit. The STS Forum was still underway at the cutoff; no independent national endorsement pages, signature sheet, implementation annex, common budget, governance charter or operating programme were located.",
  "use_note": "PDFs control over extractions. The archive-capture and GovInfo CET PDFs are distinct official representations. August 17 is verified NSSTS public availability, not a proven publication or Congressional-transmission timestamp. Exclude doctrine synthesis, implementation state, funding, authorization, awards, facilities, deployment and inferred operating consequences. The document assertion that it satisfies 42 U.S.C. 19221 is citable as document content; actual submission timing and compliance remain unresolved.",
